cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite it."
title: "FAIR in action — a metadata model and toolkit for infection-omics projects"
abstract: >-
  A machine-readable core metadata model with assay profiles (scRNA-seq, bulk/dual
  RNA-seq, LC-MS/MS proteomics, flow cytometry), from which a metadata-capture app,
  gap-sheets, validators, repository exporters and a bronze/silver/gold FAIR audit
  are generated. Every field is tagged by who can supply it — machine, project, or
  human — so that researchers are asked only for what nobody else can know.
